Ladybird anchors a text chunk by the least and the greatest position its
characters cover, as the text layout algorithm of SVG 2 has it. Blink
does the same in SvgTextLayoutAlgorithm::ApplyAnchoring(), and Gecko in
SVGTextFrame::DoAnchoring(): In Chrome 157.0.8103.79 and Firefox 151.0,
the new test gives the same character positions as in Ladybird. WebKit
26.5 anchors a chunk by where its last character ends instead, so it
gives other positions for each case in the test.
